      {
        "id": 70184,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-11T21:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>You can definitely feel free to gather and share any data you wish, and we'll definitely take a look!</span></p></blockquote><p><span>Challenge accepted. &nbsp;First step is to have some iconified cards for people to test out. &nbsp;In one afternoon of Photoshopping, here's what I came up with as <a href=\"http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/files/iconified_voss.zip\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">an iconified Grand Warlord Voss deck</a>&nbsp;(Voss having almost nothing but cards with start- or end-of-turn effects). &nbsp;I've replicated the entire deck so that people can just print it out and play with it to see how the icons affect their experience.</span></p><p><span>The cards look just like the official printed cards except I didn't bother to put the flavor text on there (sue me), but it does have the art. &nbsp;I didn't want them to be stripped-down art-less cards, because that would affect the experiment. &nbsp;If you ended up hating playing with these cards, was it because of the icons, or because they were hoopty art-less versions? &nbsp;Hopefully that won't be an issue.</span></p><p><span>Replicating full decks&nbsp;</span><span>feels dangerously close to copyright infringement, but I rationalize it by pointing out that you can't play the game with just a Voss deck alone, so hopefully it's not so bad. &nbsp;If anyone official wants me to remove the file, of course I will.</span></p><p><span>The cards have the \"SV:\" and \"EV:\" symbols to indicate when an effect happens at the start or end of the villain phase. &nbsp;Players should assume that they were made aware of the meaning of these symbols when they read the instruction manual for the game and not try to puzzle out the mystery of what an \"S\" next to a \"V\" could possibly mean in the game. ;)</span></p><p><span>I'm particularly please with how the TCF spaceships and the villain card looks. &nbsp;They have both start- and end-of-turn effects on the card, and the SV and EV icons clean their cards up so much. &nbsp;Very easy to see what you need to do on those cards now.</span></p><p><span>I went a little further and added a green shield icon to cards which have a damage reduction effect, and a red explosion icon to cards which give a damage boost. &nbsp;I'm not as certain about the benefits of these icons, but since these are common effects which you need to be able to remember every time you deal or receive damage, I figured I'd toss them on there to see how it went. &nbsp;There could be any number of icons to represent things you should remember in the game, but I didn't want to go too crazy. &nbsp;If people decide that even these two are too much, they're easily removable.</span></p><p><span>(I'd love to be able to do something about the wordiness of \"the hero target with the highest hp\" too, but we're taking baby steps here.)</span></p><p>Please don't get hung up on the fact that I used red and green colors for the icons. &nbsp;These aren't any kind of a finished product, and I know they're troublesome for some colorblind people. &nbsp;If it turned out that everyone loved the icons so much that &gt;G reprinted every single deck with icons tomorrow, I'd assume that they'd choose a more appropriate color. &nbsp;For my slapped-together Voss cards, I went with the obvious red and green.</p><p>So, print them out (hopefully in color, but if not, maybe you can highlight the icons to add the effect a color version would have), play with them a couple of times, and let's hear of your experiences.</p>",
        "post_number": 75,
